{"id":"bbca861320d80dbfe2bf2b3f8e809a6e96f2f5b9","axis":"silent","repo":"systemd/systemd","sha":"bbca861320d80dbfe2bf2b3f8e809a6e96f2f5b9","parsed":{"files":[{"path":"man/systemd-nspawn.xml","lines":["@@ -1973,10 +1973,16 @@ After=sys-subsystem-net-devices-ens1.device</programlisting>"," ","           <para>Note: when <command>systemd-nspawn</command> runs as systemd system service it can propagate","           the credentials it received via <varname>LoadCredential=</varname>/<varname>SetCredential=</varname>","-          to the container payload. A systemd service manager running as PID 1 in the container can further","-          propagate them to the services it itself starts. It is thus possible to easily propagate credentials","-          from a parent service manager to a container manager service and from there into its payload. This","-          can even be done recursively.</para>","+          to the container payload, if they are passed on with","+          <option>--load-credential=<replaceable>ID</replaceable>:<replaceable>ID</replaceable></option>,","+          i.e. if <replaceable>PATH</replaceable> is the name of a credential rather than a path. A systemd","+          service manager running as PID 1 in the container can further propagate them to the services it","+          itself starts. It is thus possible to easily propagate credentials from a parent service manager to a","+          container manager service and from there into its payload. This can even be done recursively. For","+          <filename>systemd-nspawn@.service</filename>, credentials may also be passed with the","+          <varname>SetCredential=</varname> and <varname>LoadCredential=</varname> settings in","+          <citerefentry><refentrytitle>systemd.nspawn</refentrytitle><manvolnum>5</manvolnum></citerefentry>","+          files.</para>"," ","           <para>In order to embed binary data into the credential data for <option>--set-credential=</option>,","           use C-style escaping (i.e. <literal>\\n</literal> to embed a newline, or <literal>\\x00</literal> to"],"additions":10,"deletions":4,"truncated":false},{"path":"man/systemd.nspawn.xml","lines":["@@ -352,6 +352,43 @@","         <xi:include href=\"version-info.xml\" xpointer=\"v261\"/></listitem>","       </varlistentry>"," ","+      <varlistentry>","+        <term><varname>SetCredential=</varname></term>","+        <term><varname>LoadCredential=</varname></term>","+","+        <listitem><para>Pass a credential to the container. These settings are equivalent to the","+        <option>--set-credential=</option> and <option>--load-credential=</option> command line switches,","+        and take <replaceable>ID</replaceable>:<replaceable>VALUE</replaceable> and","+        <replaceable>ID</replaceable>:<replaceable>PATH</replaceable> respectively, where","+        <replaceable>PATH</replaceable> is either an absolute path or the name of a credential passed to","+        <command>systemd-nspawn</command> itself. Each may be specified more than once to pass multiple","+        credentials. If the same credential ID is assigned more than once by the same setting, the last","+        assignment takes effect. If the empty string is assigned, the list of credentials set by the","+        respective setting so far is reset. Credentials from the settings file and from the command line are","+        not combined: if any credential is passed on the command line, these settings are ignored, unless","+        <option>--settings=override</option> is used, in which case the credentials from the settings file","+        replace those from the command line. See","+        <citerefentry><refentrytitle>systemd-nspawn</refentrytitle><manvolnum>1</manvolnum></citerefentry> for","+        details.</para>","+","+        <para>As with the settings of the same names in unit files (see","+        <citerefentry><refentrytitle>systemd.exec</refentrytitle><manvolnum>5</manvolnum></citerefentry>),","+        if the same credential ID is specified with both settings, <varname>LoadCredential=</varname> takes","+        priority, and <varname>SetCredential=</varname> acts as a fallback if the file does not exist. A","+        credential that is to be inherited from <command>systemd-nspawn</command> itself, i.e. if","+        <replaceable>PATH</replaceable> is a credential name, is skipped if it was not passed. In both of","+        these cases, a missing credential is not considered fatal.</para>","+","+        <para><varname>LoadCredential=</varname> is privileged (see above), as it reads files on the host.","+        For example, the credentials of <filename>systemd-nspawn@.service</filename> may be propagated to","+        the container with <literal>LoadCredential=<replaceable>ID</replaceable>:<replaceable>ID</replaceable></literal>","+        in a settings file in <filename>/etc/systemd/nspawn/</filename>. Do not use","+        <varname>SetCredential=</varname> for secret data, as settings files are usually readable by","+        unprivileged users. Use <varname>LoadCredential=</varname> instead.</para>","+","+        <xi:include href=\"version-info.xml\" xpointer=\"v263\"/></listitem>","+      </varlistentry>","+","       <varlistentry>","         <term><varname>LimitCPU=</varname></term>","         <term><varname>LimitFSIZE=</varname></term>"],"additions":37,"deletions":0,"truncated":false},{"path":"src/nspawn/nspawn-gperf.gperf","lines":["@@ -62,6 +62,8 @@ Exec.LinkJournal,             config_parse_link_journal,              0,"," Exec.Timezone,                config_parse_timezone_mode,             0,                        offsetof(Settings, timezone)"," Exec.SuppressSync,            config_parse_tristate,                  0,                        offsetof(Settings, suppress_sync)"," Exec.RestrictAddressFamilies, config_parse_restrict_address_families, 0,                        0","+Exec.SetCredential,           config_parse_set_credential,            0,                        0","+Exec.LoadCredential,          config_parse_load_credential,           0,                        0"," Files.ReadOnly,               config_parse_tristate,                  0,                        offsetof(Settings, read_only)"," Files.Volatile,               config_parse_volatile_mode,             0,                        offsetof(Settings, volatile_mode)"," Files.Bind,                   config_parse_bind,                      0,                        0"],"additions":2,"deletions":0,"truncated":false},{"path":"src/nspawn/nspawn-settings.c","lines":["@@ -6,7 +6,10 @@"," #include \"capability-list.h\""," #include \"conf-parser.h\""," #include \"cpu-set-util.h\"","+#include \"creds-util.h\"","+#include \"escape.h\""," #include \"extract-word.h\"","+#include \"memory-util.h\""," #include \"namespace-util.h\""," #include \"nspawn-expose-ports.h\""," #include \"nspawn-mount.h\"","@@ -14,6 +17,7 @@"," #include \"nspawn-settings.h\""," #include \"parse-helpers.h\""," #include \"parse-util.h\"","+#include \"path-util.h\""," #include \"process-util.h\""," #include \"rlimit-util.h\""," #include \"set.h\"","@@ -142,6 +146,8 @@ Settings* settings_free(Settings *s) {","         free(s->hostname);","         cpu_set_done(&s->cpu_set);","         set_free(s->restrict_address_families);","+        machine_credential_context_done(&s->credentials);","+        strv_free(s->load_credentials);","         strv_free(s->bind_user);","         free(s->bind_user_shell);"," ","@@ -1093,3 +1099,132 @@ int config_parse_restrict_address_families("," ","         return 0;"," }","+","+int config_parse_set_credential(","+                const char *unit,","+                const char *filename,","+                unsigned line,","+                const char *section,","+                unsigned section_line,","+                const char *lvalue,","+                int ltype,","+                const char *rvalue,","+                void *data,","+                void *userdata) {","+","+        Settings *settings = ASSERT_PTR(data);","+        _cleanup_(erase_and_freep) char *value = NULL;","+        _cleanup_free_ char *id = NULL;","+        const char *p;","+        ssize_t l;","+        int r;","+","+        assert(rvalue);","+","+        /* Don't log the assignment or the data on failure, they might be secret. */","+","+        if (isempty(rvalue)) {","+                machine_credential_context_done(&settings->credentials);","+                settings->credentials = (MachineCredentialContext) {};","+                return 0;","+        }","+","+        r = machine_credential_split(rvalue, &id, &p);","+        if (r == -ENOMEM)","+                return log_oom();","+        if (r < 0) {","+                log_syntax(unit, LOG_WARNING, filename, line, r, \"Invalid credential assignment, ignoring.\");","+                return 0;","+        }","+","+        if (!credential_name_valid(id)) {","+                log_syntax(unit, LOG_WARNING, filename, line, 0, \"Credential name is not valid, ignoring: %s\", id);","+                return 0;","+        }","+","+        l = cunescape(p, UNESCAPE_ACCEPT_NUL, &value);","+        if (l == -ENOMEM)","+                return log_oom();","+        if (l < 0) {","+                log_syntax(unit, LOG_WARNING, filename, line, l, \"Failed to unescape data of credential '%s', ignoring: %m\", id);","+                return 0;","+        }","+","+        /* As in unit files, a later assignment overrides an earlier one for the same credential. */","+        MachineCredential *cred = machine_credential_find(&settings->credentials, id);","+        if (cred) {","+                erase_and_free(cred->data);","+                cred->data = TAKE_PTR(value);","+                cred->size = l;","+                return 0;","+        }","+","+        r = machine_credential_add(&settings->credentials, id, value, l);","+        if (r < 0)","+                return log_oom();","+","+        return 0;","+}","+","+int config_parse_load_credential(","+                const char *unit,","+                const char *filename,","+                unsigned line,","+                const char *section,","+                unsigned section_line,","+                const char *lvalue,","+                int ltype,","+                const char *rvalue,","+                void *data,","+                void *userdata) {","+","+        Settings *settings = ASSERT_PTR(data);","+        _cleanup_free_ char *id = NULL, *source = NULL;","+        const char *p;","+        int r;","+","+        assert(rvalue);","+","+        /* The credentials are only loaded once we know that the settings file is trusted, hence only","+         * validate the syntax for now. */","+","+        if (isempty(rvalue)) {","+                settings->load_credentials = strv_free(settings->load_credentials);","+                return 0;","+        }","+","+        r = machine_credential_split(rvalue, &id, &p);","+        if (r == -ENOMEM)","+                return log_oom();","+        if (r < 0) {","+                log_syntax(unit, LOG_WARNING, filename, line, r, \"Invalid credential assignment, ignoring: %s\", rvalue);","+                return 0;","+        }","+","+        if (!credential_name_valid(id)) {","+                log_syntax(unit, LOG_WARNING, filename, line, 0, \"Credential name is not valid, ignoring: %s\", id);","+                return 0;","+        }","+","+        if (path_is_absolute(p) ? !path_is_normalized(p) : !credential_name_valid(p)) {","+                log_syntax(unit, LOG_WARNING, filename, line, 0,","+                           \"Credential source is neither a normalized absolute path nor a credential name, ignoring: %s\", p);","+                return 0;","+        }","+","+        source = strdup(p);","+        if (!source)","+                return log_oom();","+","+        /* As in unit files, a later assignment overrides an earlier one for the same credential. */","+        STRV_FOREACH_PAIR(i, s, settings->load_credentials)","+                if (streq(*i, id)) {","+                        free_and_replace(*s, source);","+                        return 0;","+                }","+","+        if (strv_consume_pair(&settings->load_credentials, TAKE_PTR(id), TAKE_PTR(source)) < 0)","+                return log_oom();","+","+        return 0;","+}"],"additions":135,"deletions":0,"truncated":false},{"path":"src/nspawn/nspawn-settings.h","lines":["@@ -7,6 +7,7 @@"," #include \"conf-parser-forward.h\""," #include \"cpu-set-util.h\""," #include \"forward.h\"","+#include \"machine-credential.h\""," #include \"rlimit-util.h\""," #include \"seccomp-util.h\""," #include \"volatile-util.h\"","@@ -195,6 +196,8 @@ typedef struct Settings {","         int suppress_sync;","         Set *restrict_address_families;","         bool restrict_address_families_is_allowlist;","+        MachineCredentialContext credentials;","+        char **load_credentials; /* pairs of credential ID and source */"," ","         /* [Files] */","         int read_only;","@@ -283,6 +286,8 @@ CONFIG_PARSER_PROTOTYPE(config_parse_userns_ownership);"," CONFIG_PARSER_PROTOTYPE(config_parse_bind_user);"," CONFIG_PARSER_PROTOTYPE(config_parse_bind_user_shell);"," CONFIG_PARSER_PROTOTYPE(config_parse_restrict_address_families);","+CONFIG_PARSER_PROTOTYPE(config_parse_set_credential);","+CONFIG_PARSER_PROTOTYPE(config_parse_load_credential);"," "," DECLARE_STRING_TABLE_LOOKUP(resolv_conf_mode, ResolvConfMode);"," "],"additions":5,"deletions":0,"truncated":false},{"path":"src/nspawn/nspawn.c","lines":["@@ -65,6 +65,7 @@"," #include \"image-policy.h\""," #include \"in-addr-util.h\""," #include \"io-util.h\"","+#include \"iovec-util.h\""," #include \"libmount-util.h\""," #include \"log.h\""," #include \"loop-util.h\"","@@ -4754,6 +4755,73 @@ static int ptyfwd_hotkey(PTYForward *f, char c, void *userdata) {","         return 0;"," }"," ","+static int merge_settings_credentials(Settings *setti